# Pinned tracebloc/client-runtime commit that
# internal/resources/envelope_contract.json is vendored from. The vendoring
# MECHANISM is backend#2220; this pin records WHICH revision the copy is, and
# that is the whole point of the file — a reader must be able to tell, from the
# vendored contract plus this ref, which number is current (backend#2580).
#
# The pinned commit is where client-runtime's runtime behaviour caught up to
# what the CLI already reads: DEFAULT_JOB_RESOURCES defaults to the contract
# FLOOR (1 CPU / 2 GiB), not the historical 2 CPU / 8 GiB `fallback_literal`
# (backend#2254, client-runtime#406). So DefaultTraining()'s floor-derived value
# and the runtime's fallback agree, and the still-present `fallback_literal` key
# is what it says it is — the retired envelope, not a live number.
#
# The vendored artifact is therefore contract_version 2: the vm_reserve/topology
# block from backend#2221 rode along, but the CLI decodes none of it — only
# overhead, floor and the single-node vectors, all byte-identical to v1.
#
# Pin, don't float — the same rule scripts/.client-ref and
# scripts/.data-ingestors-ref follow: an unrelated client-runtime commit must
# not redden every open CLI PR. The weekly run catches a pin gone stale.
#
# To adopt an upstream contract change:
#   1. cp <client-runtime>/envelope_contract.json internal/resources/
#   2. update the SHA below
#   3. go test ./internal/resources/... — the golden vectors WILL have moved
